 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+\\phantom{6}5x-\\phantom{6}2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,14x-2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,19 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+7 \\\\  & 2x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+\\phantom{6}5x-\\phantom{6}2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,14x-2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{14x-21}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,19 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $3x+7\\,$ and $\\,14x-21.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0411c5d-b798-576c-9063-a08e3c6615e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+12-\\frac{8}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476552} {:answer/id #uuid "a3bb9d15-c479-5aca-9dbb-ed0a6d1795dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+11+\\frac{7}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476561} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eedbca-0e88-5e5f-bbf2-30b15a6fb325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-13+\\frac{5}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476647} {:answer/id #uuid "e965a6b8-f562-532c-875e-a3bdc36d1264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-14-\\frac{6}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476723} {:answer/id #uuid "edf23cb8-350f-5c93-a781-ac22fc443294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+10-\\frac{4}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bb9d15-c479-5aca-9dbb-ed0a6d1795dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+11+\\frac{7}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476561} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e5fb3aa-3a5e-5f42-bac6-2ecaea522399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a96f6f0f-6a25-5d78-9b53-87a39a12c4cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-114148" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}+8x-4$ by the linear binomial $x-1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+11,$ and\n\n- the remainder $7.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=3x+11+\\frac{7}{x-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6409232-2d31-593b-90bb-8a5813883aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+48\\,$ and $\\,48x-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399825} {:answer/id #uuid "8add39dc-99a4-5ff4-9055-09c5f3363d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-24\\,$ and $\\,24x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399826} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8cd1cd-1378-56d5-a7ab-7daa3b9b05fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+30\\,$ and $\\,30x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399827} {:answer/id #uuid "29edcf41-1ad2-52f3-ab8d-9b28e983225b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-36\\,$ and $\\,48x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399828} {:answer/id #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399829} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb0dafe-c8dd-5892-9eb8-f305e87ca008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3536c096-9c19-5ecb-8cd6-bf3a33c8475e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114262" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}0x-\\phantom{00}4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows: \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}0x-\\phantom{00}4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da104913-e105-5612-9649-6f505b4f60e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da104913-e105-5612-9649-6f505b4f60e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476695} :answer-field/id #uuid "641dfae7-301e-52fe-a948-73200d0d1dc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55b9f63f-0b84-5385-9a32-8b1de9393d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55b9f63f-0b84-5385-9a32-8b1de9393d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476384} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddea1062-b353-5b96-a157-ce968af65b6a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d7da2ec-c6e2-53c6-957d-270bb7c7f62a" :question/math-academy-id "q-270261" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-8 \\\\  & x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}7x+\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{2}+15x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{8x-24}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$5{x}^{2}+7x+8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"70\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">$+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$x+3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$x+3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-8 \\\\  & x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}7x+\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{2}+15x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{8x-24}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $5{x}^{2}+7x+8$ by the linear binomial $x+3$ gives\n\n- the quotient $5x-8,$ and\n\n- the remainder $32.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+7x+8}{x+3}=5x-8+\\frac{32}{x+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c01b52c-bca9-512b-9f6e-d7dd4ecd8424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2}-3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c01b52c-bca9-512b-9f6e-d7dd4ecd8424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2}-3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476262} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e2d59ef-e005-55b3-a36c-a89aee007073" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82bb9b44-a65f-583d-86e0-2c7bd8170473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82bb9b44-a65f-583d-86e0-2c7bd8170473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476490} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b8c8237-9806-5c39-b08e-87d13938a5f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5af2aa37-0f1c-5389-a626-d55c509b3ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-320867" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"140\">$4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"120\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">$+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"140\">$x+1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">$x+1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $4{x}^{2}-3x+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder $9.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11}{x+1}=4{x}^{2}-3x+2+\\frac{9}{x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12bd1910-cd28-55d6-ad47-7d4efd790c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476233} {:answer/id #uuid "40d27e4e-5da2-5e29-9896-bf0fb45e24dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+5x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476345} {:answer/id #uuid "707eeaf7-54c2-5d0f-a7e0-80cba3b7f0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+5x-3+\\frac{7}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476454} {:answer/id #uuid "90cb12aa-021d-559e-b6bb-ac69e1cef925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476513} {:answer/id #uuid "de3d8739-eec5-5417-82f9-7d3ac2747630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+3x+5-\\frac{3}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90cb12aa-021d-559e-b6bb-ac69e1cef925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476513} :answer-field/id #uuid "44f26335-8a65-57cc-abc1-46e970937d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83ab4791-b4e2-54a9-99f4-adcd30bf75de" :question/math-academy-id "q-37893" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3$ by the linear binomial $5x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $2{x}^{2}+5x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $0.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3+\\frac{0}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129117 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01812b21-4ce2-59ad-94e3-558e8e94b2b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x+13\\,$ a